# CHAPTER 1 · The Stairwell
## The body

// Example built from the worked example in the LimOut Script spec (v0.1).
@alias neu = neutral

@macro free_arrives
[BG stairwell]
[MIRIAM neutral]
[F neu, enters from right]
+ met: FREE
@end

[CG bruno body]
[SOUND breath]
Behind me someone breathes hard through their nose.

@free_arrives
Mr. Free, from the seventh floor, in his coat, with his briefcase.
He looks at Mr. Bruno the way you look at a wrong receipt.

FREE: Go back upstairs.

He doesn't look at me. Nobody ever looks at me, and that's what I like best.

[MUSIC guest]
[MIRIAM copying FREE]
(as FREE) Weight on the right foot.
(as FREE) Eyes a little above things, as if everything cost too much.
+ copied: FREE
(as FREE) I think: Bruno knew about the fifth floor. | He does.

M(F): The fifth floor.

[MUSIC building]
[FREE scared]
[SHAKE]
FREE: What did you say?
- Who told you that?

[MIRIAM neutral]
[FREE leaves fast]
+ evidence: fifth floor
(hollow) ~One, two, three.~

## The stairs

? Do I follow him?
> Follow Free upstairs (+ flag: followed_free)
    I go up two steps behind him. He doesn't notice.
> Stay with Mr. Bruno
    I stay. Somebody has to.

IF followed_free
    On the seventh floor his door is already closing.
END

[T C, close]
TONY: I came in at [[half past twelve | He says it smoothly, like a coin sliding into the right slot.]]
“Emergency services, what's your emergency?”

>> INVESTIGATE: At the bottom of the stairwell [CG bruno body]
  * The glasses (important, + evidence: glasses)
      Intact. The lenses, the thin frame, the arms folded neatly.
  * The keys
      His bunch of keys, hooked to his belt.
  - empty: White marble. Clean, as always.
  - done: I've seen enough.

>> MIND: TONY
  sign: His thumb turns the crown of his watch, back and forth.
  sign (false): His shoes are untied.
  feels: fear / grief / *excitement* / boredom
  thinks: I've never seen that old man before. / *Only I know.* / I have to get out of here.

>> PRESENT: If Mr. Bruno fell on his own, what doesn't add up?
  answer: glasses
  thud: The thud says he fell. I already know that. It doesn't say how.
  else: No. It's not this.

[Free comes down slowly, the neon flickers twice, then the music drops out]
